WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.530
- It's the holidays friends.

00:00:01.530 --> 00:00:03.510
So to celebrate, here's
some of our favorite

00:00:03.510 --> 00:00:05.830
new and returning TV and streaming picks

00:00:05.830 --> 00:00:08.000
that are sure to put you
in the spirit of the season

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:09.860
on this week's Binge Guide.

00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:11.070
Oh, the holidays.

00:00:11.070 --> 00:00:13.630
It's time for cozy clothes,
face fulls of food,

00:00:13.630 --> 00:00:16.170
and lots and lots of movie and TV shows

00:00:16.170 --> 00:00:17.830
for your annual holiday Binge.

00:00:17.830 --> 00:00:20.550
And although there are tons
of classic holiday options,

00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:22.160
we think that these brand new titles

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:24.250
are sure to bring you
some much needed cheer

00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:25.430
this holiday season.

00:00:25.430 --> 00:00:27.550
So, in no particular
order, here are our picks

00:00:27.550 --> 00:00:29.920
for the best new holiday themed shows

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:31.460
and streaming movies of the year,

00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:34.290
starting with the new Hulu
film, "Happiest Season."

00:00:34.290 --> 00:00:38.180
This heartfelt and hilarious
rom-com stars, Kristen Stewart

00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:39.910
and Mackenzie Davis, as her girlfriend,

00:00:39.910 --> 00:00:41.520
who has yet to come out to her parents,

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:43.440
who the two visit for Christmas.

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:45.460
And with tons of heartfelt moments,

00:00:45.460 --> 00:00:47.470
it adds a much needed queer-take

00:00:47.470 --> 00:00:49.860
on the traditional home
for the holidays storyline.

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:51.107
Critics have called the film quote,

00:00:51.107 --> 00:00:53.867
"An utter delight with more
than enough holiday cheer

00:00:53.867 --> 00:00:55.247
"that should be added to the list

00:00:55.247 --> 00:00:57.030
"of holiday season staples."

00:00:57.030 --> 00:00:59.750
You can watch this one in
just an hour and 42 minutes,

00:00:59.750 --> 00:01:02.410
but it'll leave a smile
on your face for days.

00:01:02.410 --> 00:01:05.157
And next on our list is
the Netflix family film,

00:01:05.157 --> 00:01:07.100
"Jingle Jangle: A Christmas Journey".

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:09.090
Keegan-Michael Key and
Forest Whitaker star

00:01:09.090 --> 00:01:12.080
in this musical fantasy about
a down on his luck toy maker

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:13.730
who gets back in the groove

00:01:13.730 --> 00:01:15.040
with the help of his granddaughter

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:16.950
and lots of song and dance.

00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:19.420
The film redefines what a
Christmas musical can be.

00:01:19.420 --> 00:01:21.810
With nine original songs
including one written

00:01:21.810 --> 00:01:24.480
by Grammy winner, John Legend,
critics say "Jingle Jangle"

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:27.010
is a holiday adventure
with an uplifting message

00:01:27.010 --> 00:01:28.990
that celebrates the yule-tide season.

00:01:28.990 --> 00:01:31.020
And at just two hours long,
you could just put this one

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:32.630
on repeat and you'll have yourself

00:01:32.630 --> 00:01:34.480
a merry little Christmas soundtrack.

00:01:34.480 --> 00:01:36.847
Another holiday must
binge is the new series,

00:01:36.847 --> 00:01:38.080
"Dash and Lily".

00:01:38.080 --> 00:01:40.700
This Netflix series seems
like typical young adult fare

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:43.170
with beautiful well-to-do
older teens running

00:01:43.170 --> 00:01:44.620
around New York city in winter,

00:01:44.620 --> 00:01:47.520
but don't judge the red
note book by its cover.

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:49.810
Look closer and you'll
find a charming show

00:01:49.810 --> 00:01:51.710
filled to the brim with holiday cheer,

00:01:51.710 --> 00:01:54.430
lovable characters, and
some great rom-com moments

00:01:54.430 --> 00:01:56.810
that'll melt even the coldest of hearts.

00:01:56.810 --> 00:01:59.240
At a perfect 100% on the tomato meter,

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:00.970
critics all agree that "Dash and Lily"

00:02:00.970 --> 00:02:02.810
is a delightful rom-com adventure

00:02:02.810 --> 00:02:04.900
with plenty of holiday cheer.

00:02:04.900 --> 00:02:06.410
The whole season can be binged

00:02:06.410 --> 00:02:07.880
in just under three 3 1/2 hours,

00:02:07.880 --> 00:02:10.250
which makes it the perfect
jolt of Christmas spirit

00:02:10.250 --> 00:02:11.740
for anyone who needs it.

00:02:11.740 --> 00:02:13.510
And we're gonna throw a dose of reality TV

00:02:13.510 --> 00:02:14.987
into the mix with our next pick,

00:02:14.987 --> 00:02:17.130
"The Great Christmas Light Fight".

00:02:17.130 --> 00:02:20.330
This feel-good competition
show first debuted in 2013

00:02:20.330 --> 00:02:23.730
and aims to find the best,
brightest, and most awe-inspiring

00:02:23.730 --> 00:02:26.200
Christmas light decorations
around the country.

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:28.330
From traditional snowmen and reindeer

00:02:28.330 --> 00:02:31.530
to elaborate custom builds
with robots or pyrotechnics,

00:02:31.530 --> 00:02:33.860
this show is sure to
inspire you and your family

00:02:33.860 --> 00:02:36.390
with the contestants'
creativity and passion

00:02:36.390 --> 00:02:37.830
for spreading holiday cheer.

00:02:37.830 --> 00:02:40.310
And while we don't have a
critic's consensus for the show,

00:02:40.310 --> 00:02:42.610
we can say that fans of cooking, crafting,

00:02:42.610 --> 00:02:44.920
and home renovation shows will find plenty

00:02:44.920 --> 00:02:46.600
to love on "Light Fight".

00:02:46.600 --> 00:02:48.440
And with eight seasons, bingeing this show

00:02:48.440 --> 00:02:50.270
will keep you busy for 45 hours,

00:02:50.270 --> 00:02:51.870
but you'll have more than enough inspo

00:02:51.870 --> 00:02:53.939
for your next light decoration project.

00:02:53.939 --> 00:02:56.197
And last, but certainly not least is

00:02:56.197 --> 00:02:58.270
"The Christmas Chronicles" Part Two".

00:02:58.270 --> 00:03:01.220
Directed by a holiday movie
maestro, Christopher Columbus,

00:03:01.220 --> 00:03:03.260
the Netflix film stars real-life couple,

00:03:03.260 --> 00:03:04.530
Kurt Russell and Goldie Hawn

00:03:04.530 --> 00:03:06.540
as Mr. and Mrs. Claus, which should be

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:09.330
all the recommendation
necessary, but the show backs up

00:03:09.330 --> 00:03:11.650
the big names with big
heart, Christmas magic,

00:03:11.650 --> 00:03:15.040
and classic holiday
sentimentality in spades.

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:16.930
Critics say "The Christmas
Chronicles: Part Two"

00:03:16.930 --> 00:03:18.760
is more engaging than the first film,

00:03:18.760 --> 00:03:21.160
and is a sweet second
helping of holiday cheer

00:03:21.160 --> 00:03:23.600
that fans of the first
will certainly enjoy.

00:03:23.600 --> 00:03:25.710
And while you could just stream part two

00:03:25.710 --> 00:03:28.510
in about two hours, you
should start with part one

00:03:28.510 --> 00:03:30.900
to get the full Christmas
Chronicles experience

00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:34.010
which will take you an
extra hour and 45 minutes.

00:03:34.010 --> 00:03:36.500
All right, friends, now you've
got plenty of titles to add

00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:38.720
to your nice list and
maybe some new favorites

00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:40.740
that you can come back to year after year.

00:03:40.740 --> 00:03:43.750
For even more holiday TV and
streaming recommendations,

00:03:43.750 --> 00:03:45.900
be sure to check out rottentomatoes.com.

00:03:45.900 --> 00:03:48.230
And be sure to check out the
new Rotten Tomatoes Is Wrong,

00:03:48.230 --> 00:03:51.080
a podcast from Rotten Tomatoes,
because fresh and rotten

00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:52.780
is just the beginning of the conversation.

00:03:52.780 --> 00:03:55.230
And new episodes drop every Thursday.

00:03:55.230 --> 00:03:56.470
And we'll see you guys back here

00:03:56.470 --> 00:03:57.920
for more recommendations based

00:03:57.920 --> 00:03:59.650
around the movies and shows that you love

00:03:59.650 --> 00:04:01.981
right here on the Rotten
Tomatoes Binge Guide.

00:04:01.981 --> 00:04:04.564
(upbeat music)

